# Future work — features/editor/chrome

- `overlayRect` under CSS `zoom`. The conversion in `manuscript-overlay.ts`
  mixes two coordinate spaces that agree today and would stop agreeing the
  moment a manuscript ancestor carried `zoom`: `getBoundingClientRect()` is
  zoom-scaled, while `clientLeft`/`clientTop` and `scrollLeft`/`scrollTop` are
  not. A Chromium probe at `zoom: 1.25` missed the target by 73px across and
  48.125px down; ordinary LTR scrolling and negative-`scrollLeft` RTL scrolling
  were exact. No manuscript ancestor is zoomed or transformed today, so this is
  a trap rather than a bug. If editor zoom ever ships, `overlayRect` needs an
  explicit scale conversion and a real-browser test to hold it — a jsdom suite
  stubs both readings and would agree with whatever the code does.
